    50	for profiling. Missing tools limit performance claims and add no mandatory run
    51	or admission gate. See the [profiling workflow](cookbook/workflows/profile-cuda-bottlenecks-with-nsight-systems.md).
    52	
    53	**Evaluate generality and keep custody.** Report win rate and bank margin across
    54	different opponents with version, seed, seat, denominator, legality, completion
    55	and runtime. Distinguish selection from held-out qualification. Preserve stable
    56	experiment identity with separate attempt/checkpoint metadata, compact local
    57	source-bound evidence and W&B telemetry using v3 identifiers. Telemetry outages
    58	remain visible. Keep credentials, bulk weights/corpora and local state out of
    59	git with custody manifests; preserve source and lockfiles. The owner decides
    60	submission. No old v2 score, ranking, lane mandate or pod allocation transfers.
    61	
    62	## Retained starter engineering workflow
    63	
    64	## Repository Map
    65	
    66	- Start with `README.md` for setup, fixture regeneration, and the current
    67	  reference episode IDs.
    68	- Use `docs/rules-engine.md` for rules-engine architecture, current status,
    69	  and known rule risks before changing `src/rules_engine/`.
    70	- Use `docs/rules-parity-coverage.md` as the parity coverage source of truth.
    71	  Update it whenever rules behavior, fixtures, or coverage changes.
    72	- Reference `docs/rl-api-specs.md` before changing `python/owl/rl.py`, `src/rl/`, or
    73	  public RL tensor shapes.
    74	- Reference `docs/model-architecture.md` before changing `python/owl/model/` or model
    75	  config, tensor ordering, actor, critic, or initialization behavior.
    76	- Reference `README.md` and the training config tests before changing
    77	  `python/owl/train/`, `scripts/run_ppo.py`, or `configs/train/`.
    78	- Reference `docs/pr-checklist.md` before creating, recommending, or merging a PR.
    79	
    80	## Development Workflow
    81	
    82	- Run `just py-prepare` / `just rs-prepare` after any `python` / `rust` code edits, respectively. This handles formatting, linting, static type-checking, and tests.
    83	- Run `just prepare` before creating or recommending a commit or PR.
    84	- Leave touched code in better shape than you found it, while keeping cleanup
    85	  scoped to the task at hand.
    86	- Add dependencies with `uv add` / `cargo add`; don't edit `.toml` or `.lock` files directly when adding dependencies.
    87	- Keep `Cargo.lock` and `uv.lock` tracked. Update lockfiles with package-manager
    88	  commands, not manual edits.
    89	- Avoid jumping through hoops for backwards compatibility - don't be afraid of
    90	  refactoring and breaking old APIs in order to improve them.
    91	- Before creating or recommending a PR, complete `docs/pr-checklist.md` and summarize any residual risks.
    92	- Merge PRs with a regular merge commit by default. Do not squash-merge unless
    93	  the user explicitly requests it.
    94	- For retained Orbit Wars rules changes, keep `docs/rules-engine.md` and
    95	  `docs/rules-parity-coverage.md` current with implementation state, test
    96	  surface, and known gaps.
    97	- `just docs-fresh` requires mapped code changes to update their mapped docs.
    98	  If docs are already current for a small change, rerun the check with
    99	  `DOCS_CURRENT=1` to indicate that the mapped docs were reviewed and are
   100	  still current.
   101	
   102	## Error Handling
   103	
   104	- Fail fast with explicit, informative errors instead of silent fallbacks.
   105	- When user input is invalid, raise clear exceptions.
   106	- For persisted data schemas owned by this repo, prefer strict key access and explicit validation over backward-compatibility fallbacks.
   107	
   108	## Attribute Access
   109	
   110	- Avoid `getattr`, `setattr`, and `__dict__` in first-class code paths. They
   111	  undermine the repo's mypy-forward pseudo-typed style; prefer direct attribute
   112	  access and explicit union narrowing with `isinstance`.
   113	- Use dynamic attribute access only for narrow, deliberate cases such as
   114	  iterating over known schema/dataclass fields (`ObsBatch.model_fields`,
   115	  `_OBS_TENSOR_FIELDS`) or test monkeypatching. If backwards compatibility
   116	  seems to require dynamic access, prefer explicit schema migration and record the reason.
   117	
   118	## Cookbook contract
   119	
   120	**Read first.** Read `cookbook/index.md`, the newest `cookbook/log.md`, and
   121	relevant notes at the start of work. Search concepts, synonyms and negative
   122	evidence before creating knowledge or repeating an approach. Read governing
   123	notes citing an edited file as a `repository:` source; if a first-edit hook
   124	presents one, read it and explicitly retry the intended edit.
   125	
   126	**Work in bounded changes.** State a target and observable completion/stopping
   127	condition. Keep change/run artifacts in `ops/`; git preserves implementation
   128	history. Report checks and unknowns without inventing thresholds or results.
   129	
   130	**Record every adaptation.** Owner: “every adaption you made to this repo, please
   131	add a cookbook record.” Every material repository adaptation must have an
   132	identified cookbook record linking changed paths, reason, actual checks and
   133	remaining gaps. Coherent adaptations may share a contract record with an explicit
   134	inventory. This overrides the generic progress-only exemption for adaptations;
   135	routine monitoring still belongs in working artifacts.
   136	
   137	**Record before finishing.** Material decisions, corrections and reusable
   138	findings require three edits together: note, its folder `index.md`, and a
   139	prepended `cookbook/log.md` entry.
   140	
   141	- Keep routine launch, build, checkpoint and monitor output in the change's
   142	  working artifacts. Close result episodes with outcomes, denominators and gaps;
   143	  freeze completed evidence. Progress alone earns no new durable note.
   144	- Revise an existing durable concept when its reusable claim, evidence,
   145	  consequence or limits change. Reconcile its opening, conclusion, metadata and
   146	  index description together. Replace superseded current prose and link history;
   147	  do not append dated operational progress to References.
   148	- Split independent claims when needed. Preserve unique dirty history and incoming
   149	  links before moving it. Keep indexes to links/descriptions and logs to what
   150	  changed, why and a link.
   151	
   152	**Declare provenance.** Every concept requires `type`, `title`, `description`,
   153	`tags`, `status`, `generated`; first tag `kaggriculture-v3`. Reserved index/log
   154	files are exempt; a register declaring fields is not. A Decision quotes its
   155	decider and identifies the source. Never make an interpretation into owner
   156	adoption. Verification names an actual check of this version; status alone proves
   157	nothing. Repository sources are literal single-line
   158	`repository:<repo-root-relative-path>` values with forward slashes and no `.`
   159	or `..` segments. Keep external sources in their own namespace. Shape/source
   160	lint cannot establish truth, completeness or applicability.
   161	
   162	**Promote supported knowledge.** Name an independent source/check, future
   163	consequence and existing-concept search before promotion. Unsupported findings
   164	stay in working evidence. A Lesson needs at least two supporting episodes.
   165	Review after each episode or monthly, whichever is rarer; repair retrieval and
   166	contradicted claims in place. Add a typed folder only with its first real note.
   167	
   168	**One current board, when warranted.** Once there are two results to rank, keep
   169	one living Decision `cookbook/decisions/the-kaggriculture-v3-board.md`: dated
   170	position, ranked options with evidence and loss conditions, scoped tombstones.
   171	Read the full board before opening an episode and say which option is pulled and
   172	why. Changes to its facts require four edits together: note, index, log, board.
   173	Keep the whole board within 12,000 JavaScript UTF-16 code units, replacing current
   174	state and linking history. Preserve byte-exact dirty history and checksums before
   175	removal. No empty day-one board or imported v2 ranking.
   176	
   177	**Keep the view derived.** Root `kaggriculture-v3.base` sits beside `cookbook/`;
   178	the vault symlinks them as `cookbook/kaggriculture-v3.base` and
   179	`cookbook/kaggriculture-v3`. Scope by folder and exclude index/log basenames.
   180	
   181	Claude/Codex hooks restore context, gate the first governed edit, lint writes and
   182	check corrections; Git pre-commit checks staged note sources plus staged log.
   183	Direct script checks are distinct from harness discovery and trust. See
   184	[setup receipt](ops/cookbook-setup-checks.md) for exact verification limits.
