     9	# Kaggriculture v3
    10	
    11	Use this repository as the Isaiah starter adapted to Kaggriculture. Preserve its
    12	license, useful training infrastructure and development workflow. Read the
    13	[cookbook scope](cookbook/decisions/v3-reuses-isaiah-infrastructure-with-kaggriculture-semantics.md).
    14	Historical Orbit Wars docs describe the retained starter; they do not establish
    15	Kaggriculture rules or port completion. Keep `scripts/run_ppo.py` the canonical
    16	trainer and extend its shared path instead of creating a second trainer. The
    17	owner explicitly requires the current v3 data pipeline (Rust I/O and PPO): keep
    18	the starter's Rust/PyO3 caller-owned buffers and existing PPO loop canonical;
    19	reuse v2 engine semantics behind the v3 adapter, not its collector/trainer.
    20	**Do not take the v2 model implementation.** Reuse starter transformer blocks and
    21	new game stems/heads. V2 reward shaping (economic penalties, bank difference,
    22	win/loss/draw) may be adapted with explicit coefficients, critic-range and
    23	bootstrap semantics; no unmeasured reward recipe is presumed optimal.
    24	
    25	**Architecture and debugging.** Map investment payback, labor allocation, sale
    26	timing and market adaptation through legal observation, representation, choice
    27	and executable action. Make behavior reproducible and localizable. Before a run,
    28	state its supported mechanism or diagnostic question, inputs/code path, expected
    29	discriminating observation and stopping condition. Diagnose information,
    30	decision, execution and architecture errors separately; name unresolved
    31	attribution. When repairs stall, inspect the engine and relevant primary sources
    32	before spending again; record supported limits and reopening conditions. No blind
    33	experiments or uninspectable systems; this is reasoning, not an approval gate.
    34	
    35	**Stateless observation-only policy.** Actions use explicit current-observation
    36	tokens. No between-turn hidden state, temporal memory training or new history
    37	tokens. Within-turn autoregressive prefix state resets on each observation.
    38	Opponent identity may not condition actor/critic inputs, embeddings, heads,
    39	losses, rewards, normalization or checkpoint selection. Collection mixes and
    40	panel labels are allowed without exposing identity to the model. Reject
    41	prohibited checkpoint state. Follow the [adopted constraints](cookbook/decisions/the-policy-is-stateless-and-observation-only.md).
    42	
    43	**Correct high throughput is required.** Measure equivalent complete work,
    44	including valid learner turns per full update and phase costs; distinguish
    45	startup, hardware, precision and workload changes. Component speed does not
    46	prove end-to-end speed. For NVIDIA CUDA bottlenecks, **Nsight Systems (`nsys`)
    47	is the canonical timeline profiler**; reuse representative captures or profile
    48	a bounded relevant phase. Preserve versions, source/config identity, trace paths,
    49	overhead and limits. Do not disrupt a learner, upgrade drivers or weaken security
    50	for profiling. Missing tools limit performance claims and add no mandatory run
    51	or admission gate. See the [profiling workflow](cookbook/workflows/profile-cuda-bottlenecks-with-nsight-systems.md).
    52	
    53	**Evaluate generality and keep custody.** Report win rate and bank margin across
    54	different opponents with version, seed, seat, denominator, legality, completion
    55	and runtime. Distinguish selection from held-out qualification. Preserve stable
    56	experiment identity with separate attempt/checkpoint metadata, compact local
    57	source-bound evidence and W&B telemetry using v3 identifiers. Telemetry outages
    58	remain visible. Keep credentials, bulk weights/corpora and local state out of
    59	git with custody manifests; preserve source and lockfiles. The owner decides
    60	submission. No old v2 score, ranking, lane mandate or pod allocation transfers.
