     1	# Brief — Task 2.3: Kaggriculture grammar action heads (Claude), v3
     2	
     3	Plan: Task 2.3; contract v4 "Action"; C11 (rebuilt, using the reference's batched heads as design and test oracle); I0b; L6. Reviewer: Codex. Real mask tables come from the native grammar (Task 1.2, Codex). Until it lands, the heads are developed against a typed table interface with small synthetic tables, and the integration test waits for 1.2.
     4	
     5	This v3 replaces v1 and v2 as the operative text. Review history: `codex/brief-2.3-review.md` (v1, REVISE) and `codex/brief-2.3-rereview.md` (v2, REVISE). Reference line numbers refer to `kg/reference-2026-09-29`.
     6	
     7	## 1. Topology (Isaiah's actor blocks; the heads are the only game-specific part)
     8	
     9	- **`actor_input_proj: nn.Linear(3D, D)`** over `[entity ‖ self player ‖ plan]`, following Isaiah's `source_actor_input_proj` pattern. For unit frames the entity is `own_actor_hidden[:, a]`; for market frames it is the plan hidden (there is no market entity), as in the reference. **Muon-eligible**, as in Isaiah's model.
    10	- **`actor: KaggricultureGrammarActor(nn.Module)`** holds everything game-specific:
    11	  - `source_norm: LayerNorm` (Isaiah's actor normalizes its input)
    12	  - `market_position: nn.Embedding(11, D)` (queue position)
    13	  - `slot_embeddings: nn.ModuleDict` for within-frame prefix conditioning: `unit_kind 20`, `unit_item 16`, `unit_quantity_present 2`, `unit_quantity_high 32`, `market_kind 8`, `market_item 16`, `market_quantity_high 32`
    14	  - `heads: nn.ModuleDict` of `OutputProjectionMLP(trunk_cfg, width)` for the 9 sampled slots: `unit_kind`, `unit_item`, `unit_quantity_present`, `unit_quantity_high`, `unit_quantity`, `market_kind`, `market_item`, `market_quantity_high`, `market_quantity`
    15	- **Implicit slots:**
    16	  - slot 0 `unit_actor`: the frame ordinal
    17	  - slot 2 `unit_target`: reserved, always 0
    18	  - slot 11 `stop`: set on the STOP frame only
    19	
    20	  All three have zero density.
    21	- **Conditioning:** `hidden_stage = base + prefix / sqrt(stage + 1)`, where `prefix` sums the embeddings of the slots already chosen in the frame (the reference factorization, rebuilt).
    22	- **Initialization and optimizer wiring (explicit):**
    23	  - `get_input_layers` returns `market_position.weight` and each slot embedding's `.weight` as parameters. `reset_parameters` initializes them as Isaiah's token parameters (normal, std `D^-0.5`). Isaiah's `_init_input_layer` only handles `nn.Linear` / `nn.Parameter`, so the weights are passed, not the `nn.Embedding` modules.
    24	  - `reset_parameters` is extended beyond the current critic-only output reset: every actor `head.out` goes through `_init_linear(..., gain=_ACTOR_HEAD_INIT_GAIN = 0.01)`, giving orthogonal weights and zero bias. Every `head.out` is also returned by `get_output_layers`.
    25	  - `actor_input_proj.weight` and every head's `.up.weight` stay Muon-eligible. The embeddings, `head.out`, norms and biases go to AdamW.
    26	
    27	## 2. Grammar tables and masks
    28	
    29	`GrammarTables` (typed; built by `python/owl/kaggriculture/gpu_grammar.py`, ported from `gpu_sampling_grammar.py` (C7) and extracted from the native plans (C3, Task 1.2)). `δ0(W)` is a width-`W` mask admitting only 0.
    30	
    31	| Slot | Stored table | Effective mask |
    32	|---|---|---|
    33	| 1 `unit_kind` | `unit_kind [20]` | `where(unit_live[..., None], unit_kind, δ0(20))` |
    34	| 3 `unit_item` | `unit_item [20,16]` | `unit_item[kind]` |
    35	| 4 `unit_quantity_present` | `unit_quantity_present [20,2]` | `unit_quantity_present[kind]` |
    36	| 5 `unit_quantity_high` | `unit_quantity_high [2,32]` | `unit_quantity_high[present]` |
    37	| 6 `unit_quantity` | `unit_quantity_low [2,2,32]` | `unit_quantity_low[present, (high == 0).long()]` |
    38	| 7 `market_kind` | `market_kind [8]` | `where(available[..., None], market_kind, δ0(8))`, then HIRE removed where capacity is exhausted |
    39	| 8 `market_item` | `market_item [8,16]` | `market_item[kind]` |
    40	| 9 `market_quantity_high` | `market_quantity [8,32]` | `market_quantity[kind]` |
    41	| 10 `market_quantity` | `market_quantity [8,32]` | `market_quantity[kind]` |
    42	
    43	Expected supports (from `myolie_sampler.rs:147–258` `State::allows`/`advance` and reference `kaggriculture.py:578–675`; the implementer re-derives them, and a test compares every table with the native plans):
    44	
    45	- **Unit kind:** `1..18`.
    46	- **Unit item:** `1..12` for kinds 6/7, `1..5` for kind 8, otherwise `{0}`.
    47	- **Unit quantity:**
    48	  - Only kinds 6/7 allow `present = 1`.
    49	  - Absent quantity forces both digits to 0.
    50	  - Present quantity excludes low digit 0 only when the high digit is 0.
    51	- **Market item:** `1..5`, `{1, 9}`, `10..12` and `1..9` for kinds 3, 4, 5, 6; otherwise `{0}`.
    52	- **Market quantity digits:** `0..31` for kinds 3–6, otherwise `{0}`. The extractor asserts that the high- and low-digit supports are equal. Rust moves kinds 4–6 into their quantity-bearing state after slot 8.
    53	
    54	## 3. Runtime grammar context and frame placement
    55	
    56	The actor receives `actor_counts [B]` (own actors per row), `order_limits [B]`, `hire_limit` (config; default **241**) and `live [B]` (`still_playing`).
    57	
    58	```text
    59	unit_live[b,f]     = live[b] & (f < actor_counts[b])
    60	available[b,p]     = live[b] & (p < order_limits[b])        p = 0..10
    61	market_frame[b,p]  = actor_counts[b] + p
    62	market_live[b,p]   = live[b] & (p <= first_final_NONE[b])
    63	lengths[b]         = where(live[b], actor_counts[b] + s[b] + 1, 0)   s = STOP position
    64	```
    65	
    66	- Unavailable positions force `NONE`, including the sentinel at `p == order_limits`.
    67	- Padded unit frames use singleton-zero support.
    68	- Inactive rows produce all-zero tokens, length 0, and zero log-probs and entropies.
    69	- **HIRE capacity** counts *submitted* HIREs whether or not they would execute: HIRE is allowed at position `p` iff `actor_counts + exclusive_prefix_HIREs(p) < hire_limit`.
    70	
    71	## 4. Sampling (coupled Gumbel, exact categorical)
    72	
    73	- **Categorical draws:** exact Gumbel-max (no multinomial). Log-probs and entropies come from masked `log_softmax` over the effective mask.
    74	- **Market kind:**
    75	  - Draw **eight independent Gumbels per market position**, independent across positions.
    76	  - `raw_kind = argmax(scores)` over the initial mask.
    77	  - The **exclusive raw-HIRE prefix count** gives `can_hire`. Where capacity is exhausted, HIRE is masked and the argmax is re-taken over the **same perturbed scores** (no redraw); the corrected outcome can be `NONE` or `EMPTY`.
    78	  - Density evaluation uses the **exclusive final-HIRE prefix count** of the final kinds.
    79	- **STOP:**
    80	  - STOP is the first final `NONE`, which **keeps its kind probability** in slot 7.
    81	  - The forced sentinel at `p == order_limits` has zero density.
    82	  - Later positions are marginalized: zero log-prob and entropy.
    83	  - `EMPTY` consumes an order.
    84	
    85	## 5. Replay validation (`evaluate_actions`), after the reference `_decode` (`kaggriculture.py:747–783`)
    86	
    87	`evaluate_actions` must reject malformed programs itself, because PPO and BC replay never call native `step`. Native admission on `step` (Task 1.4) still exists as a separate guard.
    88	
    89	1. **Before any policy kernel:** check that `tokens` and `lengths` shapes are `[E,2,252,12]` / `[E,2]` and that both are `int64` (a Python-side check, no device sync).
    90	2. **Safe indexing:**
    91	   - Every replay-derived gather, table lookup and embedding index uses a clamped temporary index. The original value's validity goes into device flags.
    92	   - Repaired values are never admitted or returned. A host check after the kernels cannot undo an out-of-range access, so indices must be safe before execution.
    93	3. **Three device flag groups**, all computed in the tensor core:
    94	   - **support:** every chosen value is inside its prefix-dependent effective mask (§2 and §3).
    95	   - **length:** `lengths` equals the reconstructed `where(live, actor_counts + s + 1, 0)`.
    96	   - **canonical equality:** the reconstructed canonical token tensor equals the supplied tensor **element for element**. This covers:
    97	     - actor ordinals
    98	     - the reserved target
    99	     - unit fields in market frames and market fields in unit frames
   100	     - STOP bits
   101	     - every padding element
   102	     - all-zero tokens for inactive rows
   103	4. **One synchronization:**
   104	   - Aggregate the flags into one compact vector, then make one host transfer and branch.
   105	   - This runs outside the compiled tensor core and before the result returns to loss computation, as the reference `_check_flags:121–126` did.
   106	   - The error message names the failing group.
   107	   - `valid` stays on an explicitly typed internal policy result. `ModelOutput` gets no validity field.
   108	5. **Sampling path:** `forward` makes **no** host sync; validity there is guaranteed by construction and checked in tests. Removing that sync is a throughput choice, not the L6 corruption remedy. L6 is handled by the dispatch guard (2.1), Task 3.6's first-minibatch log-ratio alarm and Phase 6 qualification.
   109	
   110	## 6. Outputs
   111	
   112	- `KaggricultureActions(tokens [E,2,252,12], lengths [E,2])`.
   113	- **Log-probs:**
   114	  - `ModelActionLogProbs.event [E,2,252,12]`: per-frame, per-slot densities, zero for slots 0, 2 and 11.
   115	  - `per_player_entity = event.sum(-1)`
   116	  - `launch = zeros_like(per_player_entity)`
   117	- **Entropies** mirror the log-prob layout:
   118	  - `entropies.event` has the same shape.
   119	  - Its sum over slots gives `per_player_entity`.
   120	  - `components[name] = event[..., slot]`.
   121	- `ModelOutput` includes the critic values (2.2).
   122	- `evaluate_actions` replays the tokens teacher-forced through the same code path as sampling.
   123	
   124	## 7. Tests (tiny CPU; synthetic tables until 1.2)
   125	
   126	1. **Replay invariant (L6 regression shape):**
   127	   - Freeze the weights, sample once, and save tokens, lengths and per-slot log-probs and entropies, with their frame sums.
   128	   - Re-evaluate the saved actions:
   129	     - (a) as the same batch
   130	     - (b) split into minibatches of different sizes
   131	     - (c) permuted, re-batched, then restored to the original order
   132	   - Every result must match the **saved** values to ≤ 1e-5 (FP32 eager). A second `forward` is never the reference.
   133	   - Cases: dense (241 actors, 10 orders), HIRE capacity, STOP at every position, and mixed actor counts, order limits and inactive rows within one batch.
   134	2. **Masks against the native plans:**
   135	   - Every table row matches the native plans.
   136	   - Quantity cases:
   137	     - omitted unit quantity
   138	     - rejected explicit unit zero
   139	     - values `1`, `31`, `32`, `1023`
   140	     - accepted market zero
   141	3. **Gumbel exactness:** empirical frequencies of 20k draws match the masked softmax for one slot (chi-square bound).
   142	4. **HIRE coupling by enumeration** (3 positions, 8 kinds, budgets 0/1/2/3/10):
   143	   - The test drives the **actual** sampler and replay implementation.
   144	   - The enumerated joint probability of every final program equals the replayed density, and the total sums to 1 within 1e-9.
   145	   - Correction outcomes include both `NONE` and `EMPTY`.
   146	5. **STOP and marginalization:**
   147	   - Post-STOP positions contribute 0 log-prob and entropy.
   148	   - The first final `NONE` keeps its slot-7 density; the forced sentinel has zero density.
   149	   - `lengths` counts every frame including STOP.
   150	6. **Malformed-program rejection:** one test per flag group, each raising with the group named:
   151	   - out-of-support value
   152	   - wrong length
   153	   - non-canonical actor ordinal, reserved target, cross-kind field, STOP bit or padding
   154	   - nonzero inactive row
   155	   - out-of-range index (no device fault)
   156	   - wrong dtype or shape
   157	7. **Compiled density and gradient:** the reference CPU `backend="eager", fullgraph=True` density/gradient test (`tests/kaggriculture/test_model.py:483–505`), with host validation outside the captured core. Plus a finite-difference check of the `evaluate_actions` log-prob with respect to one head weight.
   158	8. **Seat isolation and statelessness** through the heads.
   159	9. **Topology and initialization:**
   160	   - `actor_input_proj` is `Linear(3D, D)` and Muon-eligible.
   161	   - The heads are `OutputProjectionMLP`, with `.up` in Muon and `.out` in AdamW.
   162	   - The embeddings live only under `actor.` and are listed by `get_input_layers` with std ≈ `D^-0.5` after reset.
   163	   - Every `head.out` has singular values = 0.01 and zero bias after `reset_parameters`.
   164	10. **Budget:** the full preset has between 6,000,000 and 10,000,000 parameters (owner decision).
   165	11. **Integration (after 1.2):** masks from the native grammar tables decode the recorded reference programs identically (oracle), and the replay invariant holds with the real tables.
   166	
   167	## 8. Out of scope and handoffs
   168	
   169	- Shared factory registration: Task 3.1.
   170	- Teacher distributions: Phase 4.
   171	- Production compiler/BF16 rollout-versus-minibatch equality and chunk-boundary checks: **Phase 6** GPU qualification. The eager test in §7.1 does not qualify the historical L6 failure; Task 3.6's pre-update log-ratio alarm is the in-run guard.

