853:## Kaggriculture
855:The Kaggriculture game uses the same shared training path through its own observation and action types. The authoritative tensor contract (shapes, dtypes, pinned enums, normalization scales, padding, environment lifecycle, rewards and the information audit against the reference encoder) is `docs/kaggriculture-contract.md`. This section only summarizes how it maps onto the shared API.
857:- **Observation** `KaggricultureObsBatch`: every row is one seat's legal view (`[env, seat]` leading dims), so rival-private state never enters the other seat's row. Named per-entity tensors mirror `ObsBatch`: tiles (200), own/rival actors (482 slots), shops (8, ordered by `shop_slot`), market products (9), `player_features` (self, opponent) and `global_features`. Categorical fields are integer indices and exact values are `int64`/`float64` side tensors.
867:- **Actions** `KaggricultureActions`: `tokens [E,2,252,12]` and `lengths [E,2]` (one unit frame per own actor, then up to `order_limits` market frames, then STOP). The slot widths and action enums are pinned in the contract; the native grammar supplies syntax/support masks.
