    10	
    11	# Explicit game tokens and grammar replace Orbit heads
    12	
    13	## Current model and adopted repair
    14	
    15	The owner rejects Python-driven autoregressive heads and directs efficient reuse
    16	of the whole Isaiah pipeline. After the scratch/plan audit found a missing
    17	independent player readout, the owner explicitly requests:
    18	
    19	> 修復差異吧 player token
    20	
    21	Source: `user-directive:2026-09-29:restore-player-token`, the direct reply to the
    22	alignment discussion. The current `batched_entities_v2` model restores that
    23	readout: one independently learned player token joins each legal seat view's
    24	scratch, plan, critic, entity and resource tokens in the reused Isaiah trunk.
    25	Initial token parameters are shared across seat views; hidden representations
    26	depend only on the relevant legal observation. No opponent identity or
    27	between-turn state is introduced.
    28	
    29	The actor input is now `[entity, player, plan]`, restoring the three Isaiah
    30	readouts. One `3D -> D` projection is evaluated as an entity term plus a shared
    31	player/plan term, with the bias included once. Market inputs use
    32	`[plan, player, plan]` before existing ordinal/field conditioning. This keeps
    33	one trunk pass and batched heads, without a GRU, frame scan, or sampled U/A
    34	coordinator. The player parameter is explicitly initialized with standard
    35	deviation `D**-0.5`, registered as an input layer, and included in token masks
    36	and work counts.
    37	
