+Question: does the coupled parallel correction have exactly the sequential law admitted by this Rust grammar? Inputs: the reference's fixed probability rows, 3 positions, 8 kinds, budgets 0/1/2/3/10. Stop when every canonical queue mass agrees within `1e-12` and both distributions sum to 1 within `1e-12`. No Monte Carlo or neural weights.
