+    None = 0, Wheat = 1, Carrot = 2, Tomato = 3, Strawberry = 4, Melon = 5,
+    Egg = 6, Milk = 7, Wool = 8, Fertilizer = 9, Goose = 10, Cow = 11, Sheep = 12,
+}
+```
+
+All enums derive `Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash`. Implement `TryFrom<i64, Error = String>` for the three token enums and `TryFrom<usize, Error = String>` for `Slot`, using exhaustive matches; no `transmute`. Expose `Slot::name(self) -> &'static str`, `Slot::width(self) -> usize`, and `as_str(self) -> &'static str` on each token enum. Uppercase command strings are exactly those in §4. `None`/`Empty` enum strings are diagnostic names; the renderer never emits `"NONE"`, `"EMPTY"` or `"STOP"` as commands. Unit 19 and items 13–15 have no enum variant and are always masked. Sources: `W:docs/kaggriculture-contract.md:193–210`; `R:engine_rs/src/myolie_sampler.rs:12–64`; `R:python/owl/kaggriculture/actor_codec.py:84–109`.
